1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
One customer-facing contract, with its semantic source and separate legal review linked at the top.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Counsel comments live in a related review document, so review material does not ship inside the contract.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,500
Complete document discovers fields and constraints from the contract's RDF and SHACL declarations.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Accepted values immediately update every connected HTML placeholder and the runtime RDF graph.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Schema.org choices select alternative legal content and reveal only the controls that now apply.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Nested choices project their selected wording into the operative clause without field-specific JavaScript.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,500
The component is generic: ontologies name the concepts, SHACL supplies the rules, and one connector correlates values.

8
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,000
Completion state can be saved separately as HTML/RDF or Turtle, then loaded through the same validation pipeline.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The RDF Navigator exposes the resulting dataset, including authored values and selected choices, as they change.
